  "contracts": [
    "types.ConvertJSONToInt chooses signed parsing only for a negative JSON string, preserves context-dependent prefix rounding and original parser/overflow diagnostics; numeric documents apply target bounds.",
    "types.ConvertJSONToFloat and ConvertJSONToDecimal apply source HandleTruncate before caller target production. Fatal JSON decimal conversion returns an unset ConvertTo datum and skips target fitting.",
    "table.castColumnValue and executor completeInsertErr/handleUpdateError retain distinct raw, INSERT, UPDATE and ODKU completion; original JSON text is never Rust Debug formatting.",
    "builtinCastJSONAsInt/Real/DecimalSig owns both scalar and vector conversion; vector evaluation completes the JSON child batch before converting selected non-NULL rows. Bit operators use the same JSON integer source conversion."
  ],
